# Skill: Starfit

> A Grok skill that grabs live Python headers by introspection, then welds bodies into a program and runs it.

## Purpose
Explain Starfit as a composer: look at real function heads, then write the bodies to match a goal. Source: fitzyracing1/skill-starfit.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Import a tool.
2. Read its live header (name, version, signature).
3. Weld a body that fits that header.
4. Run the resulting program.

## Key ideas
- Introspection (ask the running language what a tool looks like)
- Header (the name and shape of a function)
- Weld (join a body onto that shape)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/skill-starfit
header = grab_header(tool)
body = weld(header, goal)
run(body)
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. grab_header(tool) → “read the live shape of the tool”
2. weld(header, goal) → “write a body that fits both”
3. run(body) → “execute the joined program”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a header cannot be read → do not invent a fake one
- If a goal is named → weld only what that goal needs

## What a person would notice
Programs built from real tool shapes, not guessed ones.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open the HTML skill and name one goal.
